{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markov_identification","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markov_identification","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.not_markovTrace_branching_of_free_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.not_markovTrace_branching_of_free_data","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/markov_identification.lean#L152-L161","doc":"**The branching identity is refutable at freely-chosen data**, which is\nwhy it is named rather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nWith no partitions the sum is empty, so `tr_M = 1` reads `1 = 0`. Recorded as\na theorem so a later attempt to \"finish\" this file with a `sorry` fails\nagainst a standing counterexample — the third encoding of this lemma to claim\na `sorry` it did not have. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markov_identification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markov_identification","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/markov_identification.lean#L136-L150","doc":"**Clause (ii): the Markov-weighted eigenbasis sum equals the Jones–Markov\ntrace** ([`lem:feynman-markov-identification`]) — **derived**.\n\nTakes the branching identity as an explicit hypothesis and concludes the\nlemma. This is the implication the file exists to record, and it could not be\nstated while the identity was a class field the instance chose. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:feynman-markov-identification","label":"lem:feynman-markov-identification","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/feynman-markov-identification.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markovTrace_branching","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markovTrace_branching","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/markov_identification.lean#L119-L134","doc":"**The branching identity (Wenzl bridge): `tr_M = Σ_λ w_λ tr_{S_λ}`**, as a\nproposition over caller-supplied data.\n\nThe substantive content of `lem:feynman-markov-identification`: the\nJones–Markov trace decomposes as the Markov-weighted sum of Specht-module\npartial traces.\n\n**Named, not asserted.** See the module docstring for why neither a\nprojection nor a `sorry` is the honest form here, and for what the identity\nwould need in order to be derived. It is *derived* at convention D in\n`MarkovIdentificationInstance.markovTrace_branching_of_markovTrace`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.amplitudeEigenbasis_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.amplitudeEigenbasis_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/markov_identification.lean#L108-L117","doc":"**Clause (i): the amplitude is the weighted sum.**\n\nTrue by definition of `amplitudeEigenbasis`, and recorded as such — `rfl`\nconsults nothing about braids, Hecke algebras or Specht modules. Stating it\nseparately is what keeps clause (i) from being mistaken for evidence about\nclause (ii). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.amplitudeEigenbasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.amplitudeEigenbasis","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/markov_identification.lean#L102-L106","doc":"The eigenbasis transition amplitude, **defined** as the\nMarkov-weighted sum of partial traces\n`Σ_{l ∈ range nPart} w l · tr_S l`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}